  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 Contribution - The Sanergy Ltd under AADP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With this grant from the Africa Agri-food Development Programme (AADP), Sanergy Ltd intend to conduct a feasibility study in Nairobi, Kenya to establish the viability and optimimum process parameters for using local agricultural waste products (from fruit and coffee value chains) sourced from over 10,000 smallholder farmers, to produce biochar as an alternative to chemical fertilisers. The aim of the project is to create a commercially viable soil health product, affordable in local markets, that increases climate resilience by improving soil nutrient content and water retention, while providing supplementary income streams to smallholder farmers and SMEs in the agricultural processing sector.</narrative>
  </description>
